All tests pass. 

**Fix:** In `server/create.go` (`ggufLayersWithMediaType`, line 1235), the projector classification only checked for `vision.block_count > 0` (with `block_count == 0`) or `Kind() == "projector"`. New mmproj files (e.g. gemma multimodal projectors) use architecture-prefixed keys like `clip.vision.block_count` and are tagged with `general.type = "mmproj"`, so they fell through to the plain model media type.

Added one condition to the branch:

```go
} else if (f.KV().Uint("block_count") == 0 && f.KV().Uint("vision.block_count") > 0) || f.KV().Kind() == "projector" || f.KV().String("general.type") == "mmproj" {
```

`go test ./server/...` now passes, including `TestGGUFLayersClassifiesMMProjAsProjector`.
